WEBVTT

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:08.930
You're late.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.540
Why'd we have to meet here?

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.320
Sorry. I'm the one who asked everyone to come.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:18.550
Who's there?

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.000
Hey. How are ya?

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.750
Seriously?

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:30.180
Surprised to see us here?

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:33.130
The Guardian State.

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:42.770
I asked you all here because
I thought we could work together.

00:00:43.150 --> 00:00:45.050
Your sense of humor needs some work.

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:47.500
Well, I wouldn't mind.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.950
Be quiet, Tsubaki.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:53.390
I know you've been working with them.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:58.600
As a member of the Guardian State,
your thoughtless actions won't be forgiven.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:03.120
They're the ones who destroyed
the barriers protecting Tokyo.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.160
We're saving the world.

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:08.210
All fanatics say that.

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:09.580
I'm not surprised.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:14.090
The words of an organization that claims
they're protecting the country—

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:18.380
while slaying those who oppose them—
are exceptionally persuasive.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:21.060
I won't allow you to insult the Guardian State.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.850
Ichijo Julia is entering battle.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.950
Come to me, Gabriel.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:27.550
Jumonji Suruga is entering battle.

00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:29.000
Come, Lia Fáil!

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.290
You wanna fight?

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:34.380
Hey, wait!

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.260
Julie-Julie and Kotecchan, calm down!

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:41.080
Unless we destroy Tokyo,
Chaos will stain the world.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:43.990
We can save the world
without destroying Tokyo!

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.500
What?

00:01:52.330 --> 00:01:54.450
Very well. Elaborate.

00:01:54.450 --> 00:01:56.170
He's obviously lying.

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:58.410
That's right.

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:03.940
You've been destroying parts
of Tokyo because it's impossible.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.200
We can change fate.

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:11.050
Shiraki Yuri.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:45.990
Excruciating Sadness Can
Be Cured by Other Anguish

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:50.870
The agent of Chaos!

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:55.710
What is the meaning of this?

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:58.590
Wait. She's on our side!

00:03:59.790 --> 00:04:00.840
Our side?

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.300
You've been seduced by the Foundation.

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:05.920
Yuri saved Kotetsu.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:07.050
What do you mean?

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:11.940
It's true, Tsubaki-chan. I owe Shiraki-san my life.

00:04:12.590 --> 00:04:17.310
Since awakening after the Great
Collapse, I started having dreams.

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.340
Dreams of my loved ones dying.

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:24.440
First Kotetsu's dad, then Inuki-san.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:28.450
No matter how I fought,
I couldn't change the outcome.

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:30.680
Prophetic dreams of death, huh?

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:32.450
Sounds like you.

00:04:33.050 --> 00:04:35.180
Then I dreamed of Kotetsu's death.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:40.740
I gave up hope. I thought it was fate.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:43.230
But I'm still alive.

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:46.890
Yuri taught me that I can change fate.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:50.860
It's not logic or sentimentality.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:53.410
The fact that Kotetsu's still
here is all we need to know.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.490
I'm no longer at the mercy of fate.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:04:59.480
Sounds good to me.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.870
Isn't it your goal to destroy Tokyo?

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:07.360
Isn't it too late to stop?

00:05:08.020 --> 00:05:11.040
AVAL's goal is the extermination
of the Heroic Lineage.

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:15.600
To do that, they caused the Great Collapse
and are turning people into gates.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:18.930
In order to protect the Heroic Lineage,

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:23.530
Maldeus Church is trying to destroy Tokyo,
the breeding ground for said gates.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.380
There is no other way.

00:05:26.800 --> 00:05:28.640
The answer's simple, then.

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:33.160
The Heroic Lineage simply needs
to survive without destroying Tokyo.

00:05:33.870 --> 00:05:37.570
If we survive, we can stop Chaos' plan.

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:40.900
If we work together,

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:43.870
we should be able to overcome
the Foundation's attacks.

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:46.400
Not a bad idea.

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:49.080
Though we're enemies now...

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:53.270
I don't trust them.

00:05:53.780 --> 00:05:55.090
Shoko-san...

00:05:55.090 --> 00:05:58.530
The destruction of Tokyo or
the death of the Heroic Lineage.

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:00.650
It can only be one of the two.

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:04.170
Yuri had no choice but to fight,
but she joined us instead.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.220
Kotetsu was meant to die, but he was saved.

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:09.180
Fate is already beginning to change.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:13.350
You've been misled by your love affair.
For you to lecture us about fate

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:15.060
is the pinnacle of audacity.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:17.560
I just don't want anyone else to die!

00:06:18.740 --> 00:06:21.560
Help me. Please!

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:26.570
You already know my answer.

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:30.560
Maybe I'll side with Kotecchan, then.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:31.820
Akira?

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:34.540
Sure, if it means getting Haru back.

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:37.910
I'll fight with you, too.

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:40.920
Do what you want.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:45.060
We will fulfill our duty as
members of the Guardian State.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:47.760
We don't require the help of sinners.

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:56.010
Don't.

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:59.960
If you get involved, he'll dream of you next.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:03.430
I'll help.

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:05.390
You trust them?

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.740
I want to.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:13.990
Where is Yuri?!

00:07:13.990 --> 00:07:16.100
Maybe she betrayed us.

00:07:20.660 --> 00:07:23.170
Jun, have you not heard anything?

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:25.250
Nothing.

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:30.630
My daughter is a fool,
but Yuri is still useful to us.

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:32.840
Find her.

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:36.860
How could you ignore my goodwill?

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:39.780
Get involved and die, huh?

00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:43.890
It'll take more than a million
funerals to kill you.

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:46.900
I'm a tough man to kill.

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:53.370
If it lets me change the present,
I'd even work with the god of death.

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.970
There's no guarantee it'll improve things.

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:59.590
The future is based on the past.

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:01.790
If his hands are stained with blood,

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:05.000
the future he creates will
surely be bloodstained, too.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:11.750
He killed his own father so he'd survive.

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:13.580
Are you sure?

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:14.430
What?

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:16.640
Come with me.

00:08:22.850 --> 00:08:24.250
Sorry. Were you waiting long?

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:26.160
No.

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:33.450
It smells good.

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:36.870
I'm pretty confident this time.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:45.810
These are the reports from
the investigation 13 years ago.

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:50.680
When I learned Kamina Chihiro
was a vessel of Heroic Blood,

00:08:50.680 --> 00:08:52.330
I acquired them immediately.

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:55.500
The autopsy report, crime scene photos...

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:57.830
Some of this info
was never made public.

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:03.310
What you believed to be the
truth may not actually be true.

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:06.160
You're saying he <i>didn't</i> kill him?

00:09:08.190 --> 00:09:11.900
13 years ago, in a neighborhood of
summer homes in Chichibusanchu,

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:14.860
a family forced into a double
suicide was discovered.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:19.070
Their seven-year-old son was
rescued in a weakened state,

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:22.630
but the father had been dead for two weeks.

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:27.080
It's likely the son spent
all that time with the body.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.440
I... My dad...

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:41.460
I killed my dad.

00:09:42.550 --> 00:09:46.400
He fell into a coma, and when he awoke,

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:48.560
he'd lost his memories of the incident.

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:52.160
Kamina clearly said to the cops
who arrived at the scene

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:53.360
that he'd killed his father!

00:09:53.810 --> 00:09:55.640
He must've been confused.

00:09:55.640 --> 00:09:58.960
Yeah. That's what you cops thought,

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:01.620
and it was treated as a forced double suicide.

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:06.290
There were signs on Kamina Chihiro's
throat that indicated he'd been choked.

00:10:06.940 --> 00:10:08.730
His father tried to strangle him

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:11.050
but changed his mind and
stabbed himself instead.

00:10:11.050 --> 00:10:12.520
The kid stabbed him!

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:15.040
The piece of glass he used was there!

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:17.950
There were cuts on the
hand he used to hold it!

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:21.080
Kakihara, you're a journalist.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:24.470
Can you see the truth
through those warped eyes?

00:10:28.250 --> 00:10:30.650
There's information that
wasn't released to the public.

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:36.150
What was thought to be the father's
dying message was found at the scene.

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:38.640
Doesn't look like that to me.

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:44.510
My personal interpretation is that
he was trying to tell his son to live.

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:45.580
Live?

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:48.930
Yeah, right.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:50.930
It can't be.

00:10:50.930 --> 00:10:53.420
His son stabbed him.

00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:55.260
Hey, Kakihara...

00:10:56.140 --> 00:11:01.230
It's easy to tell someone to die,
but it's hard to tell them to live.

00:11:01.230 --> 00:11:06.430
Especially for someone
who's about to be killed.

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:09.560
He didn't kill him?

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:13.040
It's me.

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:16.880
Got it. Tomorrow morning.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:19.660
That was Kamina.

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:22.530
He wants us to gather at the church.

00:11:22.530 --> 00:11:25.690
I refuse. I refuse to accept this.

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:28.290
Kakihara...

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:32.960
He freed himself from the hands of
the father who tried to die with him!

00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:37.040
He refused to die with his father
and killed him instead!

00:11:40.770 --> 00:11:45.380
We know the Foundation is trying
to cause a second Great Collapse.

00:11:45.380 --> 00:11:46.810
A second Great Collapse?

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:48.230
That's no good.

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:51.350
To prepare for the Collapse,
my father has transferred

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:53.660
a number of large machines
from the research lab.

00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:55.360
What kind of machines?

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:57.110
I'm not sure.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:58.640
Where were they taken?

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:01.400
I don't know that, either. I'm sorry.

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:02.750
It's fine.

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:06.100
Knowing the Foundation's plan
is more than enough.

00:12:06.100 --> 00:12:10.410
If they cause another Great Collapse,
we'll all be turned into monsters.

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:12.290
You've been deceived.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:17.630
You're causing needless worry
so we'll fall into your trap.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:19.050
N-No!

00:12:19.650 --> 00:12:22.170
Yuri's on our side now.

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:23.720
I trust her.

00:12:24.500 --> 00:12:27.370
Me, too. She saved my life.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:30.070
Let's investigate immediately.

00:12:31.110 --> 00:12:34.120
You will regret this.

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:38.270
Everyone's so nice.

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:39.770
Yeah.

00:12:40.810 --> 00:12:43.990
Kurokami-san and her friends
are helping us now.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:46.440
It's all thanks to you.

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:49.470
It's because you saved Kotetsu.

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:52.140
Thank you.

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:56.370
I just...

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:01.240
I just wanted to help you.

00:13:02.650 --> 00:13:03.620
Yuri...

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:18.110
Did you bring it?

00:13:18.650 --> 00:13:20.650
Yeah, but...

00:13:21.270 --> 00:13:23.690
I want to remember you.

00:13:24.130 --> 00:13:27.300
There's no rush. You can take your time.

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:30.180
My memories begin with despair.

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:34.910
If I'm aiming for a new future,
I want something to support that.

00:13:36.290 --> 00:13:38.460
You said it was my mother's fault.

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:41.920
Maybe you're right.

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:45.560
But if everything began with my mom,

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:50.060
then maybe my mother's the
reason we met and were reunited.

00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:51.890
Chihiro-kun...

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:54.370
It's okay.

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:59.560
You gave me hope and the
courage to face things head on.

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:01.040
I didn't...

00:14:02.330 --> 00:14:04.790
This is my chance to regain what I lost.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:07.950
My fate is beginning to change.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:09.560
I know it is.

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:14.890
<i>The Tempest</i>, huh?

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:17.900
Your mother gave it to me.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:21.470
This came to mind first when
I was looking for keepsakes.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.920
It's my favorite book.

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:26.360
Even though they reach
the depths of despair,

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:28.580
in the end, they're all happy.

00:14:32.570 --> 00:14:36.440
"As you from crimes would pardoned be,

00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:39.170
Let your indulgence set me free."

00:14:43.410 --> 00:14:44.580
Why?

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:46.290
Why?

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:48.260
Why?

00:14:49.130 --> 00:14:50.570
Why?

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:53.530
Why won't you come home, Mitsuki?

00:14:54.310 --> 00:14:56.940
Why? Why?

00:14:57.920 --> 00:14:59.540
Why won't you come home?

00:15:00.370 --> 00:15:02.020
Have you abandoned me?

00:15:02.020 --> 00:15:04.040
Why? Why?

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:05.760
Don't abandon me.

00:15:06.630 --> 00:15:07.700
Why?

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:09.130
Why?

00:15:09.630 --> 00:15:10.600
Why?

00:15:10.600 --> 00:15:12.480
Why? Why?

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:16.220
Why did you kill your father?

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:24.540
I...

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:32.620
Recently, the AVAL Science Foundation

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:35.080
has forcibly acquired several
properties within the city.

00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:38.190
Numerous vehicles are
entering and exiting them.

00:15:38.190 --> 00:15:42.380
Are they transporting the machines
Shiraki Yuri mentioned?

00:15:43.900 --> 00:15:46.040
I'm going inside to check things out.

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:47.280
Signing off.

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:54.100
This is awful.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:05.720
This is...

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:09.890
They're artificially creating barriers.

00:16:12.370 --> 00:16:17.120
If these are at all the properties
the Foundation acquired...

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:19.580
Properties Acquired by Foundation

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:18.900
Show On Map

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:22.200
If I'm right, then...

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:26.430
Who's there?!

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:34.720
Beautiful, isn't it?

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:38.190
It's the ultimate requiem I offer up to you.

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:42.560
Are you okay, Chihiro-kun?

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:44.770
What happened?

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:48.660
You suddenly collapsed
when you touched the book.

00:16:49.930 --> 00:16:51.170
I see.

00:16:52.140 --> 00:16:53.880
Did you remember something?

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:54.980
No.

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:57.250
I see, that's too bad.

00:16:57.810 --> 00:16:58.720
Sorry.

00:17:00.020 --> 00:17:01.040
Oh, right!

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:03.130
I had another dream.

00:17:04.740 --> 00:17:05.730
Pluto!

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:09.400
I shall shatter the demon's night

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:12.840
and illuminate the dark paths of the world.

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:17.300
Death has arrived.

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:29.810
Death has arrived.

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:32.530
You think you've won?

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:35.860
You underestimate my immortal familiar.

00:17:37.070 --> 00:17:38.110
Pluto!

00:17:38.110 --> 00:17:41.370
Death to the undying.

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:44.120
Such is the reaper's scythe.

00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:45.290
This isn't over!

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:46.360
Tokotsu!

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:49.190
I shall sing your praises.

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:51.420
Death is kind to all.

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:54.260
You can't reach me from there.

00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:05.020
Death has arrived.

00:18:06.220 --> 00:18:07.620
Where's Kurokami-san?

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:09.440
We can't get a hold of her.

00:18:10.530 --> 00:18:12.320
She got what she deserved.

00:18:12.600 --> 00:18:14.970
She was deceived by the enemy's words.

00:18:14.970 --> 00:18:17.410
The Guardian State's not so special after all.

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:18.730
Shut up!

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:19.840
Where is she?!

00:18:19.840 --> 00:18:22.170
Did she say where she was investigating?!

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:23.620
Don't yell at me.

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:26.170
I let you listen to the message she left.

00:18:27.100 --> 00:18:29.800
If anything happened to her, it's your fault.

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:33.200
Chihiro-san?

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:39.620
Kurokami!

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:42.280
Wake up!

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:44.430
What happened? Kurokami!

00:18:46.580 --> 00:18:47.670
This is...

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:50.190
You found something?

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:01.450
Kurokami!

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:02.700
Marie!

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:09.950
No...

00:19:09.950 --> 00:19:14.090
We're one step closer to the
fulfillment of Chaos' ambition.

00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:17.300
Well done, Yuri-san.

00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:20.780
I didn't—

00:19:20.780 --> 00:19:24.900
Kurokami-san believed your
words and was defeated

00:19:24.900 --> 00:19:26.890
without realizing she'd been deceived.

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:29.370
No! Yuri didn't do—

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:32.800
Father.

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:37.070
Well done, my beloved daughter.

00:19:37.070 --> 00:19:38.600
It really was you.

00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:40.750
No! I didn't!

00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:42.800
You did your job.

00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:46.040
You can come home now, Yuri.

00:19:46.040 --> 00:19:48.580
Yuri will never go back to you!

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:54.960
Yuri, you can only rest easy
at your father's side.

00:19:55.230 --> 00:19:56.650
You know that.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:20:00.260
You don't belong there anymore.

00:20:00.260 --> 00:20:02.900
They're here to take you home, Yuri-san.

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:05.760
Wait! There must be some mistake!

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:10.330
Kurokami said she wanted to trust you.

00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:12.770
She wanted to trust you.

00:20:13.520 --> 00:20:15.950
If you've got any excuses, let me hear them!

00:20:15.950 --> 00:20:18.920
I never deceived her. It's true!

00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:20.400
You have to believe me!

00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:22.150
You say that <i>now</i>?

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:24.680
Marie was a good person.

00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:27.390
A really good person.

00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:32.190
Kotetsu...

00:20:33.080 --> 00:20:35.480
Come home, Yuri.

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:39.670
Please, guys.

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:41.250
Yuri is...

00:20:42.800 --> 00:20:43.970
Yuri...

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.220
Yuri!

00:20:45.910 --> 00:20:46.840
Yuri.

00:20:47.180 --> 00:20:48.840
Don't, Yuri!

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:49.680
Yuri!

00:20:50.280 --> 00:20:52.230
Wait, Yuri!

00:20:55.210 --> 00:20:56.280
Yuri...

00:21:05.850 --> 00:21:07.190
Fool!

00:21:08.190 --> 00:21:10.930
Did you think you could leave me?

00:21:11.200 --> 00:21:14.080
Though we were able to kill
one of the Heroic Lineage,

00:21:14.340 --> 00:21:16.920
I'll never forgive you for betraying me!

00:21:21.030 --> 00:21:22.590
Listen, Yuri.

00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:26.090
That place is important to Mitsuki and I.

00:21:26.390 --> 00:21:29.500
You are never permitted there!
